\pard\sl-240\slmult1 \cf1\lang1033\fs28\f0 House of the Damned\fs24 \par
\cf2 Terror grips your mind. All you can think of is to run, run... The wolves behind you are getting closer, you are certain of that. You can hear their delighted howls as if they are just behind you. You almost slip on the wet grass. It had been raining all day, but now at night it has increased to a torrent.\par
   You curse the engine failure in your car that forced you to come out and look for help. It was already darkening when you left the safety of your vehicle, and now it must surely be close to midnight. The wolves began chasing you at eleven, and for nearly an hour you have been running. Soon, surely, you will collapse...\par
   Hope! Through gaps in the trees you catch sight of a window, and in the gloom, can just make out the shape of a house. With a superhuman effort you reach the doorway, throwing it open, and once inside lean against it, panting. You hear the wolves bay outside, then the slow patter of paws as they slink away, defeated. You feel you have won.\par
   If you had known what would befall you in that house of the damned, you'd have run back outside and prayed for the wolves to come back...\par
\cf1 \par
x portraits\par
\cf2 The portrait of a pretty young girl catches your eye: Cousin Marie, 1732 - commited suicide 1764. "All she wanted was a kiss."  Thunder rumbles ominously.\par
\cf1 \par
up\par
\cf2 You move up.\par
You are on the upstairs landing of the house. A chandelier above casts a creepy glow over the room,  which is decorated in peeling green wallpaper and holds more portraits of the previous owners. Doorways go in three directions and stairs behind you lead downstairs.  You can move east, west and down.  The rain continues to batter down.\par
\cf1 \par
x portraits\par
\cf2 A particularly compelling gaze catches your eye in one of the portraits - that of "Uncle Horace, 1746-1803. Motto: I WILL LIVE AGAIN"  The wind howls and you shiver.\par
\cf1 \par
kiss marie\par
\cf2 Cousion Marie is not here!  Marie floats in from the east.  A sudden crash of lightning makes you jump.\par
\cf1 \par
kiss marie\par
\cf2 You lean forward and kiss Cousin Marie gently on the cheek. Though your lips pass through thin air, she appears to have acknowledged you for the first time: a smile spreads slowly across her grey face and she  fades away, still smiling. When she is gone completely you feel an icy sensation on your lips, and feel something pressed into your hand - a gold-set emerald.  Thunder rumbles ominously.\par
